/-!
# VOA — vertex operator algebras in Lean

This library formalizes the theory of **vertex operator algebras (VOAs)** following

> Terry Gannon, *Moonshine Beyond the Monster: The Bridge Connecting Algebra,
> Modular Forms and Physics*, Cambridge Monographs on Mathematical Physics,
> Cambridge University Press (2006).

The mathematical spine is **Chapter 5** (pp. 311–353), supported by prerequisites
from Chapters 1–3 (Virasoro algebra §3.1.2, affine algebras §3.2, lattices §1.2.1,
modular forms §2.2). Production code is `sorry`-free, and the library has no
project axiom: the two-field PBW principle `VOA.pbw` is a theorem; see `README.md`.

## Project goal

> Formalize VOAs in Lean 4, following Gannon's book, with every open input explicit.

## Layout (this file is the umbrella import)

* `VOA.Foundations` — formal distributions `𝒲⟦z^±⟧`, the formal delta,
  residues/modes, locality, OPE, the Virasoro algebra, lattices, affine Lie algebras.
* `VOA.Core` — the definitions `PreVertexAlgebra` (axioms VA1–VA5) and
  `VertexOperatorAlgebra` (axioms VOA1–VOA4), the Borcherds/Jacobi identity and its
  consequences, commutativity (Thm 5.1.4), the invariant bilinear form, the Lie
  algebra `𝒱₁`, and automorphisms.
* `VOA.Examples` — Heisenberg/free-boson, lattice, affine (WZW), and
  Virasoro VOAs.  The Moonshine module `V♮` itself is constructed in `VOA.Moonshine`
  (`VOA.Moonshine.moonshine`, with no hypotheses).
* `VOA.Modules` — weak / `ℕ`-graded / `ℂ`-graded modules, characters,
  rationality, `C₂`-cofiniteness, Zhu's algebra, fusion, contragredients.
* `VOA.Modularity` — one-point functions and chiral blocks, **Zhu's
  modularity theorem**, Jacobi characters, twisted modules and orbifolds.
* `VOA.Geometric` — out-of-scope sketches of geometric VOAs
  (spheres-with-tubes) and the chiral de Rham complex.

## Where to start reading

* `README.md` — main results, the axioms and trust base, scope and limitations, design
  decisions and naming conventions, the Gannon ⇆ Lean notation table, and the known dead ends.

## Status

The core theory, the module theory and the modularity layer are complete within their
documented scopes.  `Foundations.AffineLie` is partial: general weight-`λ` Verma nonvanishing
and the integrability of `L(λ)` are open.  The Moonshine module is constructed
(`VOA.Moonshine.moonshine`).  Four alternative invariant-form routes (`Core.InvariantFormDiagonal`,
`Core.InvariantFormFHL`, `Core.InvariantFormFHLClosure`, `Core.InvariantFormPStep`) are delimited
by conditional obstructions, and the geometric sketches are out of scope.  See `README.md`
(*Main results*, *Scope and limitations*).
-/
